      "value": "@{5e22a04eadb8896a3fa80757|full_name}: to be fair they don't necessarily allow an avatar with bounds greater than 5m. This would be user malice or ignorance by disregarding the upload limits and guides resulting in the problem you are facing. Most creators should know that an avatar that is too small or too big will cause issues with usability of the game, and the SDK for uploads throws warnings and error if you exceed certain limits that vrchat recommends. You just can't trust people to follow these as they have been bypassing these restrictions for some time.\nWhen it comes specifically to the size of the avatar there have been some issues with incorrect values being detected due to certain components so I think they had to limit the action taken by the performance system to stop avatars getting incorrectly blocked. At least in my opinion it's an unfortunate serious of events that has eventually lead to what seems to be a quest user, such as yourself, changing into an avatar that would cause issues.\nI will also point out just if you are not aware that the Minimum Displayed Performance Rank is available to avoid even being able to see such an avatar that exceeds the recommended performance values. (It just won't block your own avatar if you manually clone it to use)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
